  "synopsis": [
    {
      "langue": "en",
      "text": "Little Medusa is an action puzzle game with gameplay similar to titles like Adventures of Lolo and Kickle Cubicle. Artemiza is a goddess and the daughter of Zeus. She is also the successor to his throne on Mount Olympus. She is very vain and Fiora, the goddess of strife and magic, turns her into the gorgon Medusa. She also makes the other gods believe Artemiza has disappeared. Fiora frees the Titans and takes over the throne. Now Medusa is the only one who can stop her.\r\n\r\nThe game consists of five worlds with multiple levels and a world ends with a boss fight. Each world is tied to one of the Titans: Ariadne (water), Coeus (wind), Ermolai (earth), Fiora (magic and discord) and Thia (fire). A level consists of a single, fixed screen that is completed once Medusa has collected all yellow stars. She has two lives at the start and there are enemies roaming. She can petrify enemies with her gaze and then push them into the water to create bridges. She can also create stone blocks that serve as obstacles.\r\n\r\nSome enemies have attacks and they respawn from pots. Later levels introduce keys, chests, rotatable arrow tiles that change the movement direction of pushed enemies, and additional lives that can be picked up. The game keeps track of the score and has a timer counting down. If the game is completed quickly enough a sixth and final world is unlocked with a new ending to the story. The game has achievements and an Olympian mode with permadeath."
    },
    {
      "langue": "fr",
      "text": "Little Medusa est un jeu de puzzle d'action avec un gameplay similaire à ceux de « Adventures of Lolo » ou « Kickle Cubicle ».\r\nLa déesse Artémis, fille de Zeus et successeur du trône sur le mont Olympe est très vaniteuse. Pour la punir, Fiora, la déesse des conflits et de la magie, la transforme en Médusa et fait croire aux autres dieux qu'Artémis a disparu. Fiora libère alors les Titans et s'empare du trône. Désormais, seule Médusa a le pouvoir de l'arrêter…\r\nLe jeu comporte cinq mondes avec plusieurs niveaux et à la fin de chacun des mondes vous devrez affronter l'un des Titans libéré par Fiora : Ariadne (eau), Coeus (vent), Ermolai (terre), Thia (feu) et bien sûr Fiora (magie et discorde) elle-même."
    },
    {
      "langue": "de",
      "text": "Little Medusa ist ein Action-Puzzle-Spiel mit einem ähnlichen Gameplay wie „Adventures of Lolo“ oder „Kickle Cubicle“. Die Göttin Artemis, Tochter von Zeus und Thronfolgerin auf dem Olymp, ist sehr eitel. Um sie zu bestrafen, verwandelt Fiora, die Göttin der Konflikte und Magie, sie in Medusa und lässt die anderen Götter glauben, dass Artemis verschwunden ist. Fiora befreit dann die Titanen und erobert den Thron. Jetzt hat nur noch Medusa die Macht, sie zu stoppen... Das Spiel besteht aus fünf Welten mit mehreren Levels und am Ende jeder der Welten musst du gegen einen der von Fiora befreiten Titanen antreten: Ariadne (Wasser), Coeus (Wind), Ermolai (Erde), Thia (Feuer) und natürlich Fiora (Magie und Zwietracht) selbst."
    },
    {
      "langue": "es",
      "text": "Conviértete en una deidad polimorfa y recupera el Monte Olimpo en este juego de acción y rompecabezas. Los Titanes escaparon de sus prisiones eternas y transformaron a Artemiza, una joven diosa, en una gorgona. Ahora debe petrificar enemigos, resolver acertijos y esquivar trampas en su lucha por salvar el reino de los dioses."
    },
    {
      "langue": "it",
      "text": "Little Medusa è un puzzle game d'azione con un gameplay simile a titoli come Adventures of Lolo e Kickle Cubicle. Artemiza è una dea e figlia di Zeus. Lei è anche il successore al suo trono sul Monte Olimpo. È molto vanitosa e Fiora, la dea del conflitto e della magia, la trasforma nella gorgone Medusa. Fa anche credere agli altri dei che Artemiza sia scomparsa. Fiora libera i Titani e prende il trono. Ora Medusa è l'unica che può fermarla.\r\nnnIl gioco è composto da cinque mondi con più livelli e un mondo termina con un boss. Ogni mondo è legato a uno dei Titani: Arianna (acqua), Coeus (vento), Ermolai (terra), Fiora (magia e discordia) e Thia (fuoco)."
    }
  ],
